  imageAlt="grgaGrow garden monitoring interface with illustrated root zones, soil moisture and temperature readings"
  imageWidth={1265}
  imageHeight={712}
  title="grgaGrow — When does my lawn actually need water? — Gordan Grgić"
  description="Two probes in my 49 m² lawn send soil moisture and temperature to the cloud over Wi-Fi. The readings are public on a live page."
>
  <div class="lawn-notes" style={{ '--grow-th-light': thLiveGreen, '--grow-thp': thpLiveBlue }}>
    <header class="lawn-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow"><strong>grgaGrow</strong> / soil monitoring</p>
      <h1>When does my lawn actually need water?</h1>
      <p class="lede">I want to see how quickly the soil on my 49 m² lawn dries out in the sun and in the shade.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Since 24 November both probes are in the lawn. They share one controller, which sends their readings to the
        cloud over Wi-Fi.
      </p>
      <div id="lawn-live" class="project-actions">
        <a
          class="demo-link live-link"
          href="/demos/my-garden/?public=grgagrow"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          aria-label="Live soil readings (opens in a new tab)"
        ><span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live</a>
        <a href="#lawn-probe-service">How I found the cause</a>
        <a href="/projects/">← All project notes</a>
      </div>
      <figure id="video" class="watering-tutorial">
        <figcaption class="mila-video-label">
          <strong>One lawn, two readings</strong>
          <span>Promotional film · 3 min</span>
        </figcaption>
        <HobbyVideo
          src="/videos/grgagrow/smart-watering-en.mp4?v=20261127"
